 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Eating out in Melbourne costs more than it did a year ago, and prices have been rising faster over time.\n\n**Meals out and takeaway foods, Melbourne (annual change):**\n- **August 2026:** up 3.5% on August 2025.\n- **May 2026:** up 4.4%, the recent peak.\n- **July 2026:** up 4.1%.\n- **April 2025:** up 2.6%, so the annual rate is higher now than it was then.\n\nThe annual rate has been 3.3% or higher in every month since August 2025. The only exception is the dip to 2.5% in July 2025.\n\n**Compared with overall inflation in Melbourne:** All-groups CPI was also up 3.5% in August 2026. For most of the past year, meals out rose faster than overall prices. In May 2026 the gap was 4.4% against 3.5%, and in June it was 3.9% against 3.2%. In August 2026 the two were level.",
